From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: one unplaced node does not freeze the tree

A single node the backhaul tree could not place kept the whole tree
invalid, and mapc_sync_topology() does not run on an invalid tree. So one
node that cannot report its uplink - a MediaTek R3 agent, which answers
neither Link Metric Query nor sends our 0xE1 TLV, or any wired agent -
froze topology_link for the entire mesh at whatever it held last. Seen on
hardware 2026-09-17: the MTK box at depth -1 in dump_topology and our agent
behind it still drawn directly under the controller from a stale edge.

The tree is now valid once it is built. A node without a place keeps
depth UNKNOWN and every reader already checks that per node. The reason
the gate was added no longer holds: find_backhaul_upstream() takes the
tree path only when bh.own_iface is set, and nothing sets own_iface since
the neighbour walker went (9999993), so the bBSS fallback runs anyway.

What the DB gets for an unplaced node:
- no new edge: it has no parent to name, and naming the controller in its
  place is how phantom "-> controller" edges are made;
- its previous edge and depth are kept for NODE_UNPLACED_GRACE_S (180 s,
  monotonic), so a node that drops out for a few seconds after a restart
  or reconnect does not churn topology_link_history;
- after that the edge is dropped, which closes its history interval, and
  agent.depth becomes -1: the DB no longer claims an uplink it cannot back.

Verify: with a node that never reports an uplink in the mesh, placed
nodes still get fresh topology_link rows; the unplaced node has none (or
its old one for at most 180 s) and agent.depth -1 after that.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/cntlr.h
+++ b/src/cntlr.h
@@ -228,6 +228,11 @@ struct node {
 	 * See cntlr_bstamld_requery_due() for why re-asking is needed. */
 	uint64_t bstamld_requery_at;
 #endif
+
+	/* CLOCK_MONOTONIC seconds since the tree first failed to place this
+	 * node, 0 while it is placed (topology.c). APPEND ONLY - see the
+	 * note above. */
+	time_t unplaced_since;
 };
 
 static inline bool node_is_agent(const struct node *n)
@@ -362,6 +367,32 @@ struct node *cntlr_add_node(struct contr
 struct node *cntlr_alloc_node(struct controller *c, uint8_t *almacaddr);
 void cntlr_mark_agent(struct controller *c, struct node *n);
 struct node *cntlr_find_node(struct controller *c, uint8_t *almacaddr);
+
+/* How long a node that has lost its place in the backhaul tree keeps its
+ * last known edge and depth in the DB.
+ *
+ * A node drops out of the tree whenever its uplink is momentarily unknown -
+ * right after a controller restart, or between a reconnect and the next link
+ * metrics report - and comes back seconds later. Removing its edge at once
+ * would open and close topology_link_history intervals for nothing. A node
+ * that stays out longer than this has really lost its known uplink, and its
+ * old edge would be a claim the DB can no longer back, so it goes.
+ * Same order of magnitude as the node ageout. */
+#define NODE_UNPLACED_GRACE_S	180
+
+static inline time_t node_mono_now(void)
+{
+	struct timespec ts;
+
+	clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);
+	return ts.tv_sec;
+}
+
+static inline bool node_unplaced_expired(const struct node *n, time_t now)
+{
+	return n->unplaced_since &&
+	       now - n->unplaced_since >= NODE_UNPLACED_GRACE_S;
+}
 struct node *cntlr_find_node_with_bssid(struct controller *c, uint8_t *bssid);
 struct node *cntlr_find_node_with_sta(struct controller *c, uint8_t *stamacaddr);
 
--- a/src/db/mapc_sync.c
+++ b/src/db/mapc_sync.c
@@ -112,7 +112,8 @@ void mapc_sync_agent(struct controller *
 		"ON CONFLICT(almac) DO UPDATE SET "
 		"is_agent=excluded.is_agent, node_type=excluded.node_type, "
 		"profile=excluded.profile, multiap_caps=excluded.multiap_caps, "
-		"depth=CASE WHEN excluded.depth>=0 THEN excluded.depth ELSE depth END, "
+		"depth=CASE WHEN excluded.depth>=0 THEN excluded.depth "
+		"WHEN excluded.depth=-2 THEN -1 ELSE depth END, "
 		"uplink_type=excluded.uplink_type, "
 		"upstream_bssid=excluded.upstream_bssid, est_thput_ul=excluded.est_thput_ul, "
 		"est_thput_dl=excluded.est_thput_dl, scan_supported=excluded.scan_supported, "
@@ -139,6 +140,12 @@ void mapc_sync_agent(struct controller *
 	tdev = c->topology.valid ? topology_find_device(&c->topology, n->almacaddr)
 				 : NULL;
 	depth = tdev ? tdev->bh.depth : n->depth;
+	/* -1 keeps the last good depth (a node is often unplaced for a few
+	 * seconds); -2 tells the upsert that the node has been out of the tree
+	 * past the grace period, so its old depth is no longer true. */
+	if (tdev && depth == UNKNOWN_TREE_LEVEL &&
+	    node_unplaced_expired(n, node_mono_now()))
+		depth = -2;
 	bytes2hex(&n->ap_cap, 1, caps, sizeof(caps));	/* multiap AP-capability byte */
 
 	if (mapdb_prepare(c->db, sql, &st) != MAPDB_OK) {
@@ -820,6 +827,7 @@ void mapc_sync_topology(struct controlle
 		"depth=excluded.depth, wifi_hops=excluded.wifi_hops";
 	struct bh_topology_dev *dev = NULL;
 	mapdb_stmt *st = NULL;
+	time_t now_mono;
 
 	if (!c->db)
 		return;
@@ -833,9 +841,49 @@ void mapc_sync_topology(struct controlle
 		return;
 	}
 
-	/* Rebuild the edge set wholesale: cheap and keeps stale edges from lingering
-	 * after a re-parent. */
-	if (mapdb_exec(c->db, "DELETE FROM topology_link;") != MAPDB_OK) {
+	/* Rebuild the edge set: cheap and keeps stale edges from lingering after
+	 * a re-parent.
+	 *
+	 * Edges of placed devices are all rewritten below. A device the tree
+	 * could not place gets no edge from this sync - it has no parent to
+	 * name, and naming the controller instead is how phantom
+	 * "-> controller" edges are made. Its previous edge is kept while the
+	 * node is inside the grace period (NODE_UNPLACED_GRACE_S), so a
+	 * momentary gap does not churn topology_link_history, and dropped
+	 * after that, which closes its history interval. */
+	if (mapdb_exec(c->db, "CREATE TEMP TABLE IF NOT EXISTS topo_keep"
+			      "(almac TEXT PRIMARY KEY);") != MAPDB_OK ||
+	    mapdb_exec(c->db, "DELETE FROM topo_keep;") != MAPDB_OK) {
+		warn("mapc_sync: topology keep: %s\n", mapdb_last_error(c->db));
+		mapdb_rollback(c->db);
+		return;
+	}
+	now_mono = node_mono_now();
+	list_for_each_entry(dev, &c->topology.dev_list, list) {
+		struct node *dn;
+		char keep[18];
+
+		if (dev->bh.depth != UNKNOWN_TREE_LEVEL)
+			continue;
+		dn = cntlr_find_node(c, (uint8_t *)dev->al_macaddr);
+		if (!dn || node_unplaced_expired(dn, now_mono))
+			continue;
+
+		mac2str(dev->al_macaddr, keep);
+		st = NULL;
+		if (mapdb_prepare(c->db, "INSERT OR IGNORE INTO topo_keep(almac) "
+				  "VALUES(?)", &st) != MAPDB_OK) {
+			mapdb_rollback(c->db);
+			return;
+		}
+		mapdb_bind_text(st, 1, keep);
+		if (stmt_finish(c->db, st) != MAPDB_OK) {
+			mapdb_rollback(c->db);
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+	if (mapdb_exec(c->db, "DELETE FROM topology_link WHERE child_almac "
+			      "NOT IN (SELECT almac FROM topo_keep);") != MAPDB_OK) {
 		warn("mapc_sync: topology clear: %s\n", mapdb_last_error(c->db));
 		mapdb_rollback(c->db);
 		return;
@@ -849,6 +897,9 @@ void mapc_sync_topology(struct controlle
 		/* Skip the controller root - it has no upstream BH link. */
 		if (!memcmp(dev->al_macaddr, c->almacaddr, 6))
 			continue;
+		/* No place in the tree, or no parent to name: no edge (above). */
+		if (dev->bh.depth == UNKNOWN_TREE_LEVEL || !dev->bh.parent)
+			continue;
 
 		downstream_mac = dev->bh.own_iface ? dev->bh.own_iface->macaddr
 						   : dev->al_macaddr;
--- a/src/topology.c
+++ b/src/topology.c
@@ -83,6 +83,7 @@ void topology_build_tree_from_assoc(stru
 	struct bh_topology_dev *root, *dev;
 	struct node *n;
 	bool progress;
+	time_t now;
 
 	topology_remove_all_devices(topology);
 
@@ -139,31 +140,39 @@ void topology_build_tree_from_assoc(stru
 		}
 	} while (progress);
 
-	/* Only claim the tree is valid once every device actually found a
-	 * place in it. Anything else closes a loop we cannot get out of.
+	/* The tree is valid once it is built, even if some devices found no
+	 * place in it. A device without a place simply has depth UNKNOWN; the
+	 * readers of the tree (mapc_sync_topology, mapc_sync_agent,
+	 * cntlr_send_max_wifi_bh_hops_policy) check that per device.
 	 *
-	 * find_backhaul_upstream() (cntlr.c) consults the topology first and
-	 * only falls back to a bBSS lookup when the topology is *not* valid -
-	 * and that fallback is the sole thing that ever fills
-	 * node::upstream_bssid, which is precisely this function's input. So
-	 * declaring a tree we failed to build valid shuts the fallback off
-	 * permanently: no upstream_bssid, hence no tree, hence no
-	 * upstream_bssid.
+	 * Until 2026-09-17 a single unplaced device kept the whole tree
+	 * invalid, and mapc_sync_topology() refuses to run on an invalid tree:
+	 * one node that cannot report its uplink - a MediaTek R3 agent, which
+	 * answers neither Link Metric Query nor sends our 0xE1 TLV, or any
+	 * wired agent - froze topology_link for the entire mesh at whatever it
+	 * held last. Seen on hardware: the MTK box at depth -1 and our agent
+	 * behind it still drawn directly under the controller.
 	 *
-	 * Measured on a three-node mesh 2026-07-28: every node had
-	 * upstream_bssid all-zero and depth -1, while topology->valid was
-	 * true and topology_link held correct parents from another path.
-	 *
-	 * Leaving valid=false here is self-healing rather than a failure mode:
-	 * the next link metrics report takes the bBSS fallback, fills in
-	 * upstream_bssid, and the following rebuild places the node.
+	 * The reason that gate was put here no longer holds.
+	 * find_backhaul_upstream() only takes the tree path when
+	 * bh.own_iface is set, and nothing assigns own_iface since the
+	 * neighbour walker was removed (patch 9999993), so the bBSS fallback
+	 * that fills node::upstream_bssid runs whatever this flag says.
 	 */
 	topology->valid = true;
+	now = node_mono_now();
 	list_for_each_entry(dev, &topology->dev_list, list) {
-		if (dev->bh.depth == UNKNOWN_TREE_LEVEL) {
-			topology->valid = false;
-			break;
-		}
+		struct node *dn;
+
+		if (!memcmp(dev->al_macaddr, ctrl_al_macaddr, 6))
+			continue;
+		dn = cntlr_find_node(c, dev->al_macaddr);
+		if (!dn)
+			continue;
+		if (dev->bh.depth != UNKNOWN_TREE_LEVEL)
+			dn->unplaced_since = 0;
+		else if (!dn->unplaced_since)
+			dn->unplaced_since = now;
 	}
 
 	mapc_sync_topology(c);
